WEBVTT

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.930
The Lord of Crime murdered Whiteley.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.690
If that's true...

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.240
Miss Hudson... What's the matter?

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.950
John?

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.950
Who's this?

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.830
This is Mary Morstan.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:48.250
She works as a governess
for Mrs Forrester.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.340
I'm a little late in
announcing this to you,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.220
but we're getting married.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.100
Huh?

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.080
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.830
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:27.960
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.000
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.420
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.180
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:47.770
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:51.360
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.490
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.110
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.330
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.670
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.130
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.010
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.800
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.390
"The Sign of Mary"

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.020
"The Sign of Mary"
Mrs Forrester? The one I consulted
for about two months back?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.780
Right. After the case,
she invited us to dinner,

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.570
and I'm the only one who went, remember?
That was when I met her.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:46.700
Yes. Mrs Forrester was truly sorry to hear

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.330
that you could not come
to dinner, Mr Holmes.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.500
But I sure am glad that I went.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.550
After all, it's how I met Mary.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.850
And...?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.930
There's a matter other than
your wedding announcement

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.600
that you came to see me about, right?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.770
See here! How can you just
blurt that out, Sherlock?

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.060
Sherlock, she's just a bit nervous--

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.980
John...

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.440
Mr Holmes is correct.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.990
Huh?

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:25.870
However, I feel as though it will sound
like a rather brazen request now...

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.700
Go ahead and tell me.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.210
First off, please have a look at these.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:38.210
Astounding! I've never seen
pearls as large as those!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.550
From the size of them,

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.390
it looks like you could live for half
a year off of a single pearl.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.220
These pearls started arriving
out of the blue once per year,

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:50.980
each one on the same day,
beginning six years ago.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:54.770
No sender's name provided
on the postage slip.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.820
Would you take me through
the order of events?

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:04.700
Yes. But to do so, I must begin by
first telling you about my father.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.410
My father was an officer
who was posted to India,

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.950
and my mother passed away early on,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:15.170
so I was taken in by a
girls' boarding school.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.880
Then, ten years ago,

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.170
a telegram arrived from my father,
saying that he was home on leave,

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.420
and wished for me to come to
the hotel where he was staying.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.970
I was excited at the prospect of
our reunion, but when I arrived...

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:33.270
...my father was nowhere to be found,
his bags still in his hotel room.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:39.730
His whereabouts remain
unknown to me to this day.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:45.070
Why do you think your father's
disappearance is tied to the pearls?

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:49.240
Not long ago, I heard that whilst
my father was stationed in India,

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.870
there was a gentleman in his
regiment, a Major Sholto,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:55.170
with whom he became quite close.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.330
I thought that perhaps he
might know something,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:04.420
and when I looked up his address...
I learnt that he had passed six years ago.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:10.060
I see. The same six years ago
that your pearls began arriving.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.810
Which is why you came to think
that the two might be connected.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.690
I beg you, Mr Holmes,

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.690
I wish to know the reason for
my father's disappearance!

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.690
Would you please lend me your assistance?

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.450
All right. I'll look into it.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.830
I'm sorry, John. I did not mean
to suddenly spring this on you.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:40.420
It's all right. I'm sure Sherlock
will uncover the truth for you.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.340
Thank you.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.760
Miss Morstan is quite a charming
young lady, isn't she?

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.470
Charming? I didn't particularly notice.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:58.770
Are you joking? You didn't notice?
Don't you have any emotion at all?

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.520
Never mind me, the matter at hand is...

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:07.070
...there is still something
that she is holding back.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.240
Pondicherry Lodge?

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:18.960
An estate that Major Sholto purchased 11
years ago upon returning from India.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.800
Retired from the army, the major said
that he did well in business over there,

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.430
and is said to have come back with
a large sum of money and rare curiosities.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.890
But no matter how hard I looked,

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:34.350
I found no record of him
doing business in India.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:38.020
After his return, it's said that he
lived an extravagant lifestyle,

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:42.650
but for some reason, he became
deathly afraid of going out alone...

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.610
...and apparently, there was an incident
where he mistakenly fired a gun

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.700
at a white merchant with a wooden leg.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.620
A white man with a wooden leg?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.050
No one home?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.690
John, come on!

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.490
What the devil is it, Sherlock?!
Why are we barging in like this?!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.200
Hey, are you all right?!

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.660
Damn!

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.370
Wh-What the...?

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.710
This is finally starting
to look like a case.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.600
What has happened here?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:03.900
This must be one of Major Sholto's twin
sons, either Thaddeus or Bartholomew.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:16.410
He was quite clearly killed.
John, have a look.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:18.990
What's that? It looks like a thorn.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:22.830
It's probably a poison barb.
Definitely not of England.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.520
Who's there?!

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:50.190
You wouldn't happen to be...
Miss Mary Morstan?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.530
Huh?

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.950
What are you doing here in the mansion?

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:58.490
B-Bartholomew!

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.210
Oh, no... What's happened to you?!

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.790
You must be the twin brother, Thaddeus.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:11.000
I'll need you to tell me about the
disappearance of Mary's father,

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.300
about the pearls that were sent to her,
and the circumstances of this body.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.180
After the shooting incident,

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:23.680
my father rarely went outside again,
but then six years ago,

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:29.060
my father saw four mysterious symbols
marking the mansion's gate

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.650
and quite nearly collapsed.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:36.700
Afterward, he became bedridden,
and at last made a confession...

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.950
Th-The what?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.450
The treasure of Agra.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:44.580
That is merely one piece of it.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:48.000
I did not obtain my fortune
through business, though.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:54.380
My subordinate Morstan and I came to
possess the treasure quite unexpectedly.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.640
I resigned at once, and brought
the treasure back to England.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:04.980
A year later, Morstan also
returned and came here.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:12.570
However, Morstan and I got into a fierce
quarrel over the division of the treasure.

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:16.400
Whereupon...

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:23.910
If I had called for someone,
he may have survived.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.580
However...

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:31.630
Please, I want you to return the
treasure to Morstan's daughter.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.050
The treasure is in the mansion's...

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:40.760
It's him! He's come! Drive that man away!

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:45.310
I dashed over to the window,
but there was no one there.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:50.190
When I turned back toward the bed,
my father had already breathed his last.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:54.360
After his passing, my brother
and I searched for the treasure,

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.240
but we could not find it,

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:02.570
so at the very least, I started
sending her one pearl every year.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.700
So that is what happened.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.540
I'm so sorry, Mary.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.790
Then it really does exist...

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.210
The treasure of Agra.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:22.140
But then, just the other day,
my brother located the treasure.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.600
I can scarcely believe things
would end up like this.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:28.520
We discovered this in a safe
after our father's passing.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.230
This is Indian paper.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:36.360
It's some kind of map,
accompanied by a row of four blood seals.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:43.820
Jonathan Small, Abdullah Tonga,
John Sholto, and Arthur Morstan.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.830
Who are these other men, Small and Tonga?

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.740
I do not know.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.290
Thaddeus...

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:52.290
I want you to go to the police and tell
them everything that has transpired.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.170
R-Right.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.720
Now then...

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:03.140
This is the last point at which
we can still turn back.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:05.550
What do you mean, Sherlock?

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.680
The man that Major Sholto
was terrified by,

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:12.140
as well as the death of
his son, Bartholomew,

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:16.230
are proof positive that someone
else was after the treasure.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:20.030
Moreover, it is someone who will
go to any lengths to obtain it.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.990
We cannot guarantee Miss Morstan's
safety from this point onward.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.700
To be frank, I believe now is
the time for us to withdraw.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:31.500
Not to mention that our original design
was not to obtain the treasure.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.000
True enough. We cannot expose
Mary to any danger.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.920
I am curious as to who the culprit is,

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.840
but we <i>have </i>learnt about
her father and the pearls.

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.630
We should allow the police
to take over and go home.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.730
I...

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:55.520
I believe that as things stand,
the suspicion of Bartholomew's murder

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.230
will fall upon either ourselves
or upon Thaddeus.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.360
Huh?

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:06.110
Not only did we break into the mansion,
the door to this room was locked.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:10.790
We are the only ones who can
provide an alibi for each other,

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:15.830
and if not us, suspicion will
fall next upon Thaddeus.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:20.210
For Thaddeus's sake, as well as our own,
I think we should find the real culprit.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.590
And there it is!

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:25.300
Ostensibly, she wishes
to lend a helping hand,

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.720
but is her intent to find the treasure
in the course of catching the culprit?

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.640
Mary's object has been
the treasure from the start.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:36.690
A tainted treasure, purloined
during military service, at that.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:41.570
If she already has plans
for how to spend it,

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:45.700
then it's extremely likely that Mary
is involved in a heinous crime.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.320
If she is trying to conceal
that to marry John,

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:53.580
then I have to expose her
and reveal the truth...

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.620
...for John's sake.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:03.050
In other words, all we have to do is prove
that someone else was here, yes?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.550
In that case, we already have.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:09.930
First, there were <i>two </i>people
involved in killing Bartholomew.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.850
I observed the ground directly
beneath this room earlier.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:17.020
There were some alternating
shoeprints and round indentations.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:21.650
That was probably the wooden-legged
man that Old Man Sholto dreaded.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:26.110
And on the windowsill,
tracks from where a rope rubbed it.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.820
Judging by the footprints
left in the room,

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:33.290
the second man was smallish
and light on his feet.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:37.040
He's the one who clambered up
to the window and slipped in,

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:40.670
then lowered the box with the
treasure in it down from the room,

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:44.380
where the wooden-legged man received it.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:49.840
From all of this evidence, it is clear
that there was a third party involved.

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:54.640
Could the culprits be Small and Tonga,
the remainder of the four signatories?

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.060
What was that?

00:14:56.060 --> 00:15:00.100
My father was the officer in command
of a local battalion in India.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:06.320
If I had to surmise... I believe the two
of them were under my father's command.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:10.110
Those blood seals may have
been forged as a contract.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.570
Which would mean that Major Sholto
feared their vengeance

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:15.870
for keeping the treasure to himself.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.580
But how are we to go after the culprits?

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.210
That part is simple.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:22.170
Huh?

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:28.840
As the culprit was lowering down the box,
he accidentally broke a bottle of creosol.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:32.220
A scent that powerful will not
be so easy to wash out.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:39.020
Allow me to introduce...
a sniffer dog with an outstanding nose

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:43.310
who has led to the solution
of many a case--Toby.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:45.690
Wiggins, good show.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.150
You can kick in an after-hours bonus

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:50.990
and a contingency if he finds
what you're looking for.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.740
Whatever will I do with you?

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:59.500
Mary, would you go back to Baker Street
in the carriage that brought Wiggins?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.000
He's right.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:05.750
Let us see to tracking down the
culprits and the treasure now.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:09.260
Very well. Please do be careful.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:10.590
Mm-hmm.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.430
Right then, we're off!

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.470
Toby, off you go!

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.940
I made some coffee, Sherlock.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.610
Thanks.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:31.610
Is there any activity on the boat?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:35.910
I see steam.
They're getting ready to launch.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:40.580
Small will be arriving soon,
to make his escape.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:43.670
Once he does, we'll pursue
and capture him.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.000
Why are we going to
the trouble of a pursuit?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.510
If we arrest them before they depart,
won't that be the end of it?

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:52.050
We won't be able to keep
Mary safe that way.

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:54.380
Hmm? What are you talking about?

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.010
The man who committed
the murder is one thing,

00:16:57.010 --> 00:17:01.230
but the other's crimes of theft and
menacing are the greater challenge.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.560
After getting out of gaol in a few years,

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:10.150
if the treasure is in Mary's possession,
they will surely come to take it from her.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:13.150
So in order for us to
prevent any reprisals,

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:18.160
we need to get Small to abandon any
attachment he has to the treasure.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.700
How do you plan to do that?

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:29.710
Bingo! A white man with a
wooden leg--that one is Small!

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.380
Lestrade, we're off! After that launch!

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.680
You're sure there's a killer
aboard that boat, right?

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:40.140
Don't make me keep saying it! Hurry!

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.680
Douse the lights so they
don't see us coming!

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.940
By Jove, put yourself in my shoes,

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.020
taking a Yard police boat
without permission like this!

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:49.610
Set us off!

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.700
Distance, about 50 yards.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.330
All right, this is deep enough.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.710
Hit the lights!

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:11.250
Jonathan Small! Abdullah Tonga!

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:14.170
We know everything that you've done!

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:19.050
Hand over the treasure of Agra
that you killed Bartholomew to get!

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:23.100
Impossible! How does anyone
other than us know about that?!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.770
I <i>knew </i>there was something
amiss about you!

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:29.810
Mind your tongue! I paid you a tidy sum!
You're complicit in this!

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:33.650
Shake them if you want to stay alive!

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:36.780
Give us the treasure, nice and easy!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:42.200
D-Don't be absurd!
This treasure belongs to us!

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.540
Sherlock!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.210
Stop the boat if you want to live!

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:53.300
Damn! They mean to take the treasure
from us even if they have to kill us!

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.760
Hmm? Tonga!

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.470
Sherlock, watch out!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.480
Tonga!

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:10.270
Damn it! Oi, get us going faster!

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:14.020
This is all she can do!
The boiler is going to explode!

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:18.070
Damn it... damn it...
damn it... damn it...!

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:21.200
Damn it... Damn it...

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.200
Damn it... Damn it... Damn it...

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.290
Damn it!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:32.460
If it comes down to getting it
taken from us, I'd rather...

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:43.970
Now you'll never get your
hands on the treasure!

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:49.520
So that's why...

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.400
Yeah.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:57.190
This way, Small has voluntarily
given up his claim on the treasure.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:14.960
Small and the others' testimony was,
on the whole, just as you two inferred.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:18.460
I'm glad you caught the
criminals without incident.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:21.430
So then...

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:22.800
...where is the treasure?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.390
Mary, the thing of it is...

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.720
Small tossed it away himself.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:30.980
He thought it better than letting it
fall into another's hands

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:32.810
and cast it into the Thames.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.900
O-Oh, no...

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.900
Mary, if you had it in your possession,

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.450
Small and the others
would come after you again.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.240
We don't need any treasure.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:51.370
Without that, I...

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.250
I've been wondering all this time
why you wanted so badly

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.460
to get your hands on the treasure.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:01.630
When you heard about the existence
of the treasure from Thaddeus,

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:04.470
you did not seem too surprised.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:11.020
Which means that you knew about
the treasure, but hid that fact from us.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:13.810
Then, even after a murder
had been committed,

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:17.480
you put recovering the treasure
over your own personal safety.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:20.860
On the other hand,
you are already employed,

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:24.280
and you haven't sold a single one
of the pearls that were sent to you.

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:28.870
Meaning that you are not short
of cash for you to get by.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:33.040
Which only leaves one possibility...

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:35.170
...blackmail.

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:35.920
Huh?

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:37.000
Then I'm right.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.710
J-Just a moment!

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:42.970
Is this true? Mary, who would
be blackmailing you?

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.590
He said that if I didn't
turn over the treasure,

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:50.970
he would break up our wedding, John.

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:53.980
Who the devil told you that?!

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:59.570
There's only one man in London who would
stoop to something this underhanded--

00:21:59.570 --> 00:22:01.730
the king of blackmailers,

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:06.280
Charles Augustus... Milverton.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:14.660
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:22.880
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:33.470
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:36.850
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:40.860
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:44.230
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:51.660
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:00.250
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:14.310
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:17.100
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:22.770
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:29.450
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:50.130
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Two Criminals."
